# The control plane (the API) lives on the Cloudflare WORKER, not on Pages.
# Pages serves only the static SPA. Without these rules, Cloudflare Pages answers
# ANY unmatched path with the SPA index.html (HTTP 200) — so a misrouted
# same-origin API call (e.g. /api/workspace/resolve) receives index.html and the
# app then chokes parsing HTML as JSON ("Unexpected token '<'"), which silently
# breaks session creation. Force control-plane paths to 404 here so a stray
# same-origin call fails cleanly (the app treats 404 as "no runtime") instead of
# masquerading as a successful JSON response. Real API traffic goes to the Worker
# via its absolute origin and never touches these rules.
/api/*         /index.html   404
/global/*      /index.html   404
/workspaces/*  /index.html   404
/provider      /index.html   404
/provider/*    /index.html   404
/path          /index.html   404
/project       /index.html   404
/project/*     /index.html   404
/internal/*    /index.html   404
/.well-known/* /index.html   404

# SPA fallback for genuine app routes.
/*             /index.html   200
